---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy policy — CanYouDo?">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap-narrow">
      <p class="kicker">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="hint">Last updated: 8 August 2026</p>

      <h2 style="margin-top:36px">What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Account details</strong> — name, email, phone, postcode, and either a password (stored as a secure hash) or a Google account identifier if you sign in with Google.</li>
        <li><strong>Provider profile details</strong> — bio, area, services, hourly rate, years of experience, photos you upload, contact email and phone, availability, blocked dates, and insurance details (insurer, policy number, expiry).</li>
        <li><strong>Customer requests and bookings</strong> — dates, times, postcodes, addresses, requested areas, notes, messages, favourites and reviews.</li>
        <li><strong>Payment data</strong> — our service charge is processed by Stripe. We never see or store full card details.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 style="margin-top:32px">How we use it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To run the notice board: profiles, matching, bookings, calendars, notifications, messaging and reviews.</li>
        <li>To send transactional emails (confirmations, reminders, changes, password resets). We don't send marketing without consent.</li>
        <li>To calculate gradings from review data.</li>
        <li>Automated (AI-assisted) checks may review booking details to flag errors or misuse; anything flagged is reviewed by a human.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 style="margin-top:32px">Who sees what</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Public:</strong> a provider's display name (first name and initial), bio, area, services, photos, hourly rate and combined total, grading, review scores and review text, and whether insurance details are on file — <strong>never the policy number itself</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong>Providers with a booking:</strong> see the customer's name, address, requested areas and messages. Open notice-board requests show only the postcode, never the full address.</li>
        <li><strong>Customers with a confirmed booking:</strong> see the provider's payment details and direct contact details.</li>
        <li>Reviewers are shown as first name and initial.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 style="margin-top:32px">Where it lives</h2>
      <p>Data is stored with Supabase in the UK/EU region (London). The site is served by Netlify with Cloudflare DNS. Emails are sent via Resend. Payments are processed by Stripe. Google sign-in is provided by Google.</p>

      <h2 style="margin-top:32px">Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under UK GDPR you can request access to, correction of, or deletion of your personal data at any time. Email <a href="mailto:hello@canyoudo.uk">hello@canyoudo.uk</a> and we'll act within 30 days. Deleting your account removes your profile and photos; booking records needed for legal or accounting purposes are kept only as long as required.</p>

      <h2 style="margin-top:32px">Cookies</h2>
      <p>We use only the strictly necessary session storage needed to keep you signed in. No advertising trackers.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
